#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:58 70a7fb7eb21d4fe68ffc2a966b0a327d
msgid ""
"Get detailed metadata for SRA run accessions including sequencing "
"platform (ILLUMINA, Oxford Nano..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst a91266f0c7544821983a3ec3f5c54d12
msgid "NCBI_SRA_get_run_info tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:64 e4b1b5c7e1844ecaac23f3ac5582b236
msgid "**Name**: ``NCBI_SRA_get_run_info``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:66 3d6ae5c9effa4e75a3e374b496afb9d5
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get detailed metadata for SRA run accessions including "
"sequencing platform (ILLUMINA, Oxford Nanopore), instrument model, "
"library strategy (RNA-Seq, WGS), library source (genomic, "
"transcriptomic), library layout (paired/single), sample information, "
"study details, organism, and data statistics (total spots, bases). "
"Essential for understanding experimental design and data characteristics "
"before downloading large FASTQ files. Use SRA run accessions (SRR000001, "
"ERR000001, DRR000001) from NCBI\\_SRA\\_search\\_runs or known "
"accessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:70 312023e3896b4933ad5c61a8821968ea
msgid ""
"``operation`` (unknown) (optional) Operation type (fixed: "
"get\\_run\\_info)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:73 490c26d12c7048db9f7a4627a3890854
msgid ""
"``accessions`` (unknown) (required) SRA run accession(s) (e.g., "
"'SRR000001', 'ERR000001', 'DRR000001'). Can be single accession or array "
"of accessions. Use SRR for NCBI, ERR for ENA, DRR for DDBJ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:90 e5d783cd33e54b128534a3332a75acbd
msgid "**NCBI_SRA_link_to_biosample** (Type: NCBISRATool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:92 9180a458580f4d40a4d96006350bd13d
msgid ""
"Link SRA sequencing runs to their associated BioSample records to access "
"biological sample metada..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst 97c37c8c0b6c4ab6bfdba4ccb83ac45c
msgid "NCBI_SRA_link_to_biosample tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:98 a786249abd294fa8a18f27d1ea246c9e
msgid "**Name**: ``NCBI_SRA_link_to_biosample``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:100 3c6f503352e54f7687e2bc4ba34b8c67
msgid ""
"**Description**: Link SRA sequencing runs to their associated BioSample "
"records to access biological sample metadata including sample attributes,"
" tissue type, cell line, treatment conditions, donor information, and "
"collection details. BioSample provides rich contextual information about "
"the biological specimens used in sequencing experiments. Essential for "
"understanding experimental context and sample provenance. Returns "
"BioSample UIDs which can be used with NCBI BioSample API to retrieve "
"detailed sample metadata. Works with SRA UIDs from "
"NCBI\\_SRA\\_search\\_runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:104 c844140429384f0db1797f9c1df0a6c9
msgid ""
"``operation`` (unknown) (optional) Operation type (fixed: "
"link\\_to\\_biosample)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:107 5b478813df8d4479801cb6ba796c86aa
msgid ""
"``accessions`` (unknown) (required) SRA UID(s) from "
"NCBI\\_SRA\\_search\\_runs. Can be single UID or array of UIDs. These are"
" NCBI internal IDs (numeric), not SRR accessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:124 de80fcfdffc94d6fa70d60511c86b742
msgid "**NCBI_SRA_search_runs** (Type: NCBISRATool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:126 798c38c838e543519795647f9fe3cb62
msgid ""
"Search NCBI Sequence Read Archive (SRA) for NGS/RNA-seq sequencing runs "
"by study accession, organ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst ead363aa043a4a8da99d895b49fa4b8c
msgid "NCBI_SRA_search_runs tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:132 65e07b8a91b047feb2e481695377b1d0
msgid "**Name**: ``NCBI_SRA_search_runs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:134 baa3442986dc47a0b57d4038380a8b10
msgid ""
"**Description**: Search NCBI Sequence Read Archive (SRA) for NGS/RNA-seq "
"sequencing runs by study accession, organism, sequencing strategy (RNA-"
"Seq, WGS, ChIP-Seq), platform (ILLUMINA, OXFORD\\_NANOPORE), or library "
"source. Returns SRA UIDs which can be used with other SRA tools to "
"retrieve metadata and download links. Essential for discovering high-"
"throughput sequencing data from public repositories. Use this to find "
"relevant sequencing experiments before accessing the actual FASTQ data "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:138 3e87fef6790847a5ae9f8ca1734bd809
msgid "``operation`` (unknown) (optional) Operation type (fixed: search)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:141 00d5f7e3829f42148b8f650ffc3660cc
msgid ""
"``study`` (string) (optional) Study accession to search (e.g., "
"'SRP000001', 'ERP000001', 'DRP000001'). Searches in [Study] field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:144 9ffc8ce431de4a2c9e5bfaca49f3ebbd
msgid ""
"``organism`` (string) (optional) Organism name to filter (e.g., 'Homo "
"sapiens', 'Mus musculus', 'SARS-CoV-2'). Searches in [Organism] field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:147 7071c28ce42c4c3c9cc64a1893121489
msgid ""
"``strategy`` (string) (optional) Sequencing strategy to filter. Common "
"values: 'RNA-Seq' (transcriptomics), 'WGS' (whole genome), 'WXS' (exome),"
" 'ChIP-Seq' (chromatin), 'ATAC-Seq' (accessibility), 'Bisulfite-Seq' "
"(methylation), 'AMPLICON' (targeted), 'Hi-C' (3D genome)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:150 501af7204e80417f9503aeadcf61a105
msgid ""
"``platform`` (string) (optional) Sequencing platform to filter. Common "
"values: 'ILLUMINA', 'OXFORD\\_NANOPORE', 'PACBIO\\_SMRT', "
"'ION\\_TORRENT', 'BGISEQ'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:153 39007386d85f430485b438b70b1e9218
msgid ""
"``source`` (string) (optional) Library source to filter. Common values: "
"'GENOMIC' (DNA), 'TRANSCRIPTOMIC' (RNA), 'METAGENOMIC', "
"'METATRANSCRIPTOMIC', 'SYNTHETIC', 'VIRAL\\_RNA'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:156 f6f8bdfe8e3343c2a54fea8e86444eff
msgid ""
"``query`` (string) (optional) Free-form search query if not using "
"structured filters. Use NCBI query syntax (e.g., '(Homo "
"sapiens[Organism]) AND (RNA-Seq[Strategy])')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:159 9ec3c2f349e546bea970f3cec8e1b71c
msgid ""
"``limit`` (integer) (optional) Maximum number of results to return "
"(default: 20, max: 100)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ncbi_sra_tools.rst:162 3a04c3feb2e74c6089b40c03c675577d
msgid "``sort`` (string) (optional) Sort order for results (default: relevance)"
msgstr ""

